WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.384
In the late Three Kingdoms period, there was an old minister at the Wei court named Sima Yi.

00:00:06.384 --> 00:00:14.472
In 249, he launched a coup at Gaopingling and seized supreme power in Wei in one stroke.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:24.000
After Sima Yi died, his sons Sima Shi and Sima Zhao took power in turn, and the young emperor was sidelined.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.824
At court, the one who truly had the final say was Sima Zhao; the emperor had become a puppet with no real power.

00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:38.520
In 266, Sima Yan accepted the Wei emperor's abdication and founded the Jin dynasty.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:47.616
Cao Wei had fallen, the situation of the Three Kingdoms changed completely, and a new era began.

